title: Negotiations with the SPD
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/spd.jpg
view-if: negotiation_spd_timer = 0
on-arrival: negotiation_spd_timer = 6; month_actions += 1
tags: parliamentary_affairs

= Negotiations with the <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span>

Though they are radically different in ideology compared to us, cooperation with the <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span> is still crucial in order to better navigate the Weimar democratic system. What should we do to strengthen our ties?

- @spd: Strengthen our bonds with the Social Democratic Party.
- @cut_poor_spd: Cut consumption taxes for the poor.
- @safety_spd: Develop and enforce safety regulations.
- @lautenbach_wtb: Infuse the WTB Plan with the Lautenbach plan, with a considerable expansion of public works and wages.
- @return: Perhaps we can discuss this at a later time.
- @easy_discard

@spd
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1
go-to: dvp_op if spd_in_government = 1 and dvp_in_government = 0; spd_coalition if spd_in_government = 1 and dvp_in_government = 1; spd_op if spd_in_government = 0 and dvp_in_government = 1

@dvp_op 
on-arrival: spd_relation += 5*(1-dissent)

We are currently in opposition to the SPD-led government, but that does not preclude the general building of feelings of good will.

@spd_coalition
on-arrival: spd_relation += 8*(1-dissent)

We are currently coalition partners with them, so improving relations comes naturally.

@spd_op
on-arrival: spd_relation += 5*(1-dissent)

They are currently in opposition to our government, but that does not preclude the general building of feelings of good will.

@cut_poor_spd
subtitle: -2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -2 budget - [? if finance_minister_party != dvp_name: The <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span> does not have the Finance Ministry ?][? if lower_tax_rates < -5: Tax rates are already too low. ?]
choose-if: finance_minister_party = dvp_name and budget >= 2 and lower_tax_rates >= -5
on-arrival: spd_patience += 25 if spd_toleration; spd_relation += 5*(1-dissent)
go-to: fiscal_policy.cut_poor

@safety_spd
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span> does not have the Labor Ministry
choose-if: labor_minister_party = dvp_name
on-arrival: workers_safety += 1; labor_dissent -= 5; progressive_dissent -= 3; labor_strength += 2; progressive_strength += 1; spd_patience += 25 if spd_toleration; spd_relation += 5*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 5; workers_dvp += 3*(1-dissent); capital_strike_progress += 1 if workers_safety >= 3

The Labor Ministry works on developing and enforcing safety regulations, in order to ensure healty working conditions for the proletariat. [? if workers_safety >= 3 : Businesses have begun to argue that our focus on safety is overbearing and unnecessary, interfering with the economy. ?]

@lautenbach_wtb
unavailable-subtitle: The <span style="color: #E3000F;">**Social Democrats**</span> haven't fully formulated their plan yet.
choose-if: year >= 1932 and spd_wtb_plan
view-if: year >= 1930 and not return_to_normalcy and lautenbach_plan_adopted and not lautenbach_wtb_adopted
on-arrival: lautenbach_wtb_adopted = 1; spd_relation += 3; labor_strength += 5; progressive_strength += 5;

WIP
